            "title": "Office Depot Parent to Be Taken Private by Atlas Holdings for $842 Million",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "ODP  the parent company of Office Depot and OfficeMax, has agreed to be acquired and taken private by an affiliate of Atlas Holdings for $28 a share in cash, or $842.2 million based on its shares outstanding.  The office-supply company said Monday that the deal has been approved by its board and values the company at about $1 billion.  ODP had about 30.1 million shares outstanding and a market capitalization of $626 million as of Friday\u2019s close, according to FactSet.",
